quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  9,62,"Among them are those who hurt the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him) and say: ‘He is an ear (i.e. believes everything he hears).’ Say: ‘(He is) an ear that is good for you; he believes in Allah, trusts the believers and is a mercy for those who believe among you. As for those who hurt the Messenger of Allah, they shall have a painful punishment.’"
  9,63,"They (the hypocrites) swear to you by Allah that they might please you. But Allah, as well as His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), has a greater right that they should please Him if they are (true) believers."
  9,64,"Do they not know that whoever opposes Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), surely for him shall be the Fire of Hell, to remain there forever? That is the ultimate disgrace."
  9,65,"The hypocrites fear that a (Qur’anic) Chapter will be revealed against them, informing them about what is in their hearts. Say: ‘Keep mocking. Allah will indeed disclose what you are fearing.’"
  9,66,"If you ask them, they will certainly say: ‘We were just chatting and joking around.’ Say: ‘Were you mocking Allah, His revelations and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him)?"
  9,67,"Do not make excuses. You have disbelieved after you had believed.’ If We pardon a group of you, We shall punish another group for they have been guilty."
  9,68,"The hypocrites, both men and women, are all the same: they enjoin evil, forbid good and keep their hands shut (i.e. they remain reluctant to spend in the way of Allah). They have forgotten Allah, so He has forgotten them. The hypocrites are indeed the disobedient ones."
